:::

::: {.prose}
Using the chart above, we can do an initial categorization of flash vs burn songs. Songs in the bottom right quadrant are true "flash" songs that rise quickly up the rankings and then drop just as fast. For example, Taylor Swift's __Mr. Perfectly Fine (Taylor's Version)__ started at #90, peaked at #30 the next week, and then dropped back to #90 the next week and didn't reappear on the chart. Songs on the top right are viral hits, they climb quickly up the charts like the flashes, but they stick around and stay popular, with low decay rates. The bottom left corner is the opposite, they have slower rises up the charts, and their popularity isn't sustainable and they rapidly drop in the rankings before falling off the chart. Most songs are clustered in the top left corner, with both slow rise rates and slow decay rates. 
:::


